error[fixed_outside_a_group]: `i8[4]` is a C array member, so it stands only as a field of a `record` inside an `extern` group, whose layout a C compiler chose — here no group's record holds it (§4.19)
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-399-a-fixed-array-outside-a-group-is-told-the-repair-that-works.hero:26:17
     |
  26 | constant ZEROS: i8[4]  #~ fixed_outside_a_group
     |                 ^^^^^
  note: where it is meant for a C struct's field, that struct is a `record` inside the `extern` group of its header, and the array is written out where the record is built, as many elements as `i8[4]` says, `R(field: [a, b, …])`: no binding, constant or parameter holds a fixed array, and `[i8]` is not one
  note: where no C struct holds it, use `[i8]`, built as `[a, b, c]` or grown with `push`: it grows, it is compared and hashed like any other value, and it is what every Heroes record holds

